# Code Style Rules

**⚠️ IMPORTANT: These rules apply only to the frontend project (`frontend/`). The CMS project (`cms/`) has its own rules.**

## Prettier Configuration
- **Indentation**: 4 spaces (tabWidth: 4)
- **Quotes**: Single quotes
- **Semicolons**: Always use semicolons
- **Line Width**: 120 characters
- **Trailing Commas**: Always use trailing commas

## TypeScript Rules
- Use TypeScript for all new files
- Avoid `any` type - use proper types or `unknown`
- Use type inference where possible
- Define interfaces/types in `src/types/` for shared types
- Use strict TypeScript settings

## Naming Conventions
- **Components**: PascalCase (e.g., `UserProfile.tsx`)
- **Files**: Match component name; a utility is a camelCase folder holding `index.ts`
- **Functions/Variables**: camelCase
- **Constants**: UPPER_SNAKE_CASE
- **Types/Interfaces**: PascalCase with descriptive names

## File Organization
- One component per file
- Export default for main component
- Named exports for utilities and types
- Group related files in folders (e.g., `components/organisms/`, `components/molecules/`)
- **A component is a folder**: `Component/Component.tsx`, `Component.module.scss`, `Component.test.tsx`, and `Component.stories.tsx` where it makes sense
- **A utility is a folder**: `utils/<name>/index.ts` with `index.test.ts` beside it — never a loose `utils/<name>.ts`. The same holds under `utils/base/`, `utils/cache/`, `utils/strapi/`, `utils/hooks/` and `lib/blocks/`
- Shared types stay flat files in `src/types/`

## Tests
- Every new component and utility ships with a test next to it
- `*.test.ts` runs in Vitest's `node` project, `*.test.tsx` in the `jsdom` one
- Components render through `@testing-library/react`; prefer role/text queries over test ids
- Run with `npm run test` from `frontend/`
